{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Israel joined himself to Baal Peor.</b> From the root צמד as in paired cattle, and the meaning is that a man and woman were joined together. And there is a distinction between the language of הצמדה (joining) and the language of דבקות (cleaving), for הצמדה is not as close and bonded a connection as דבקות; and had it said וידבק ישראל, Heaven forbid, there would have been no remedy for Israel. And from this our Rabbis of blessed memory derived in Sanhedrin, chapter 'Four Modes of Execution by the Court': those who joined themselves to Baal Peor are like a thread twisted together, but Israel are not so (Deuteronomy 4:4) ״ואתם הדבקים בה' אלהיכם״ — like two palm branches bonded one to the other. In a baraita it was taught: those who joined themselves to Baal Peor were joined by means of a woman, but ״ואתם הדבקים״ — you are truly cleaving."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:58.739384926Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}